ucture: {\"parameter\": \"max_site_cover\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"%\", \"conditions\": [\"height <= 8.5 m: <=300 m2 terrace (<7.5 m frontage, BTB both sides) 80%; <=300 m2 terrace (7.5-9.5 m) 75%; <=300 m2 traditional 60%; 301-400 60%; 401-500 60%; 501-1000 60%; >1000 60%\", \"height > 8.5-12 m: 50/50/50/50/60/50/50 (sic - 60% in 401-500 m2 column)\", \"height > 12 m: N/A except 501-1000 m2 50%, >1000 m2 40%\"], \"exceptions\": [\"excludes eaves, sun shading devices, patios, balconies and other unenclosed structures (RAD5)\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'Dwelling house incl. enclosed Class 10a' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - RAD carries note 'Non-compliance with this RAD is a planning scheme matter for which Council will exercise a concurrence agency role ...'; Table 1.6.1 identifies 9.3.1 'RADs and performance outcomes identified by notes as a planning scheme matter' as the alternative provisions to QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions (Building Act s33).\nResearcher notes: Column mapping verified from raw HTML colspans (300 m2 or less spans 3 sub-columns). The 60% in the >8.5-12 m / 401-500 m2 cell is as published."}$q$::jsonb);
